WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:04.270
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.940
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:13.070
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.330
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.870
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:28.380
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:34.220
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.390
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.220
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.140
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.690
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:52.610
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.610
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.030
Won't go away

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:03.870
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.000
We believed you

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:14.840
While we stand here

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:20.010
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.170
Regardless of the age, machines don't fight wars!

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.420
Battles are...

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.380
...fought by men.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.770
Warning

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.990
I've never seen a ship like this.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.490
But why did that happen?

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.320
They have such advanced weapons,

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.280
yet they couldn't take out that plane.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.370
Your ship is amazing, truly incredible.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.380
I can see why Admiral Yamamoto is after it as well.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.460
The first wave of American planes have retreated,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.960
and the skies are now clear.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.800
The ship took a direct hit...

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.890
But it is still fully battle-operational.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.850
Damage, what do you mean?!

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.860
It's alright. The Mirai is still ok.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.900
It wasn't that big a hit.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.400
However, with that much fire and smoke,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.320
there must have been casualties...

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:30.080
Deck 2 must be... a living hell now.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.920
Emergency units, medics, to the bridge!

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.460
Lieutenant Oguri, are you alright?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.920
Kashiwabara, please take over for a while.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.590
I'll be back once I've gotten him to sick bay.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.880
Y-Yes sir!

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:16.290
BATTLE MEDICAL ROOM

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:30.760
BATTLE MEDICAL ROOM

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.890
Captain, I suggest that we use...

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.140
...a Tomahawk missile to sink the Wasp.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.730
Sink the carrier?

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.240
Kikuchi! Instead of sinking it,

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.530
we can fire a Harpoon and take out their flight deck, right?

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.780
That's not an option. In the battle of the Coral Sea,

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.080
the USS Yorktown recovered from a Japanese bomb strike...

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.210
...and was fully operational with just 3 hours of repairs.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:42.080
We can get far away from them in 3 hours!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.050
If we sink the carrier, we'll be taking more than 1000 lives!

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.840
Even if it is for self-defense,

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.340
it still doesn't give you the right to kill so many people!

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.220
Kikuchi! This isn't like you!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.220
You're losing it!

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.560
This is my recommendation to ensure our survival.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.390
We're like a wounded animal alone in the woods.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.400
We do not have any way to resupply our weapons,

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.860
and we can't run away from every ship that gets in our way.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.450
I've finally realized something this time round.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.740
Only taking defensive measures won't scare anyone away.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.750
Sitting inside the CIC,

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:21.920
we can spout off our SDF principles all we like,

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.790
but this world won't understand us.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.090
Ever since we accepted Admiral Yamamoto's...

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.960
...suggestion to dock at Yokosuka...

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.800
No, from the time we got sucked back to the past,

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.340
the Allied Forces have seen us as the enemy...

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.800
...and has attacked relentlessly.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.020
If we don't acknowledge this fact and act upon it,

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.810
we won't ever get through this alive.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:44.770
My poor judgment has brought this upon us.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.480
As this ship's Weapons Officer,

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.480
I cannot let any more of the crew get hurt,

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.490
or allow the security of this ship...

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.860
...to be compromised in any way.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:59.080
Captain, the Wasp is 250 miles to the Northeast.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.420
The Tomahawk will take about 30 minutes to get there.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.420
We've no time to lose.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.590
While it is true that we must keep all options open,

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:12.130
we can't oversimplify things and act rashly.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.090
We should send out the Umidori to keep an eye...

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.850
...on the Americans, and if we can force them to retreat,

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.890
there'll be no need for drastic actions.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.850
Yes sir!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:25.270
Communications, is the radio still working?

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.980
- Yes!
- Send a warning to the Wasp.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.570
Weapons Officer! If they call off their second attack,

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:35.320
the Tomahawk is to self-destruct.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.280
Understood.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.720
Bear Trap Open! Take off!

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.980
It's worse than I imagined.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.440
It's proof that machines and...

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.740
...technology alone don't win battles for you.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.740
A moment's error can turn the tide of war in the end.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.330
Our ship has experienced this firsthand.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.410
With the sacrifice of those who died,

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.000
we've learned an important lesson.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.010
Lieutenant Hutton was defeated by that single Cruiser?

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.760
And in less than 2 minutes?

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:42.310
That ship's anti-air defenses are much stronger than expected.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.230
That ship must be the same one from Guadalcanal.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.060
Lieutenant.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:52.320
Our second attack wave will be ready to launch in 30 minutes.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.530
Make sure there are no mistakes.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:28.270
Tomahawk... Missile away!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.150
XO! The Mirai fired a Tomahawk!

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.130
Admiral Noyes. There's been a slight delay,

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:57.630
but we'll be ready to go in 25 minutes.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.970
We just noticed that this message came in a while back.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.220
Oh?

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.140
I'm sure of it.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.230
That cruiser is the same "Sagittarius" from Guadalcanal.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.690
Our ship bears no malice towards your ship,

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:15.610
or against any of the Allied Powers in this conflict.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.610
We request that you stop your second attack upon us.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.200
If you insist on going ahead with the attack,

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.200
then we have no choice but to sink your carrier in self-defense.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.160
This sure seems like a warning to me.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.210
It's a near perfect match with the one from Guadalcanal.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.460
I don't understand. What are they trying to do?

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.260
Don't understand?

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:43.470
They are just trying to bluff their way past us.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.810
The ridiculous rumor about this invincible ship...

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.970
...has to be stopped, once and for all.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.810
But Admiral, that ship does have...

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.360
...extremely advanced weapon systems.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.480
I think we should hold off on the second assault to wait for...

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.400
...more intelligence from the planes of the first wave.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.490
- Lieutenant.
- Sir?

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.990
Scientific discoveries and Naval victories.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.500
Do you know what they both have in common?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.340
Both usually need more than one attempt...

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.500
...to be successful, don't they?

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.550
You learnt this at Annapolis, right?

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.760
You need courage to overcome your fears, Lieutenant.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.010
Sir!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.790
Fortune Inspector, Sea Fowl.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:53.040
Tomahawk proceeding at 600 feet.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.040
93 miles to target.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.250
It just passed the returning American planes.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.000
7 minutes to target.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.720
Lieutenant Satake...

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.010
I don't think the Wasp is gonna stop that second attack.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:10.010
Our warning is really just a way for us...

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.680
...to justify taking out that ship, don't you think?

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.150
Hayashibara,

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.440
without that justification, we're just...

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:23.150
And what about our crewmen who died defending the Mirai?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.490
Why are we here?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.200
And what are we protecting anyway?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.580
Lieutenant Satake,

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.210
what if... we are stuck here forever?

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.920
What should we be doing with ourselves?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.720
I'm not sure myself. All I can do now,

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.810
is hope that the Wasp will stop the second attack.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.640
Lieutenant Satake!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.650
Radar contacts.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.440
Those idiots!

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.320
American ship detected!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:08.160
A flight carrier, it must be the Wasp.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.820
It is launching its planes!

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.330
Tomahawk, time to target...

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.330
4 minutes 30 seconds.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.800
The Tomahawk's target has to be...

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.510
...the American aircraft carrier.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.970
I think they're trying to prevent a second attack on the Mirai.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.590
How big is the carrier?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.890
I need to know how many planes were sent in the first attack?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.640
About 40 planes.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.560
In that case, it has to be a Yorktown Class.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:42.650
That would mean at least 2000 men...

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.070
...would be on board right?

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.900
What's a Tomahawk?

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.410
It's an Anti-Ship Long Range missile with an...

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.200
...effective range of 310 miles.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.620
310 miles...

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.000
How strong is its warhead?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.370
I reckon one missile would be enough...

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:01.960
...to sink a Yorktown Class carrier.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:05.500
You creep! Why you!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.340
And you call yourself Japanese!?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.180
Don't you have any sense of honor as a soldier?!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:17.220
If you want to sink our ship, why don't you do it yourselves?!

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.730
You could launch your own torpedoes at the Mirai,

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.230
but I think you are too afraid of its superior firepower...

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.440
So you're getting the Americans to do your dirty work?

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:27.730
What are you trying to pull here anyway?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:31.740
To think that I made the mistake of placing my trust in you people.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:36.120
I won't let you have your way with my ship!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.330
No matter what happens now, the missile...

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.580
...from the Mirai will definitely hit the American Carrier.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.380
But that sort of thing isn't what we are here for!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.880
The Mirai's mission...

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.920
...isn't to take lives but save them!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.920
But... because of you people,

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:53.090
the Mirai was forced to play her hand and...

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.930
...take this action to defend herself!

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:03.230
Do you know that the blood of 1000 sailors is on your hands?!

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.270
Even if it is justified,

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.650
I still don't want to kill anyone.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:14.820
3 months before...

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.950
...our graduation from the National Defense Academy,

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.910
lraq ground troops switching to aerial bombing

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.950
the first Gulf War broke out in the Middle-East.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.290
We were all pretty nervous.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:24.370
Proactive contributions to the Gulf Crisis

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.590
What do you think Japan will do?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:37.600
They'll probably send Marine Sweepers for de-mining, right?

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.980
Oguri! You'll be on the Edajima soon right?

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.940
- Do us proud!
- Yes!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:50.110
And don't you guys lose the Botaoshi, okay!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.780
We're the undefeated champions for 4 years running!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.200
Leave it to us!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:58.370
The Academy students sure have it easy!

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.160
The world out there is in a mess,

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.830
and they're worried about a silly Botaoshi?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.750
What do you expect from them?

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.670
They're just a bunch of students.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.550
Just worried about themselves...

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:12.260
Kids today... have no sense of responsibility.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:18.260
We're about to graduate. Those guys aren't worth the effort.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:29.440
Alright, you guys head back to the Academy first.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:32.650
Where are you going, Kadomatsu? Some place fun?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.860
Well, something like that.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:37.280
Make you get back before curfew, alright?

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.580
Yes! We'll head back first then!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.620
Masayuki.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.750
You'll need time to change as well.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.420
- Shall we make a move?
- Yes.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.840
Yes. Kohei, you've been a great friend to us.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.920
Thank you. We have to go now.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.630
I'll walk you to the station.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:00.050
3 years and 9 months into our training,

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:05.230
Kikuchi rejected his assigned commission.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:07.310
And right before graduation,

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.060
he chose to drop out of school.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.090
Alright. You guys be sure to work hard when you're out there.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.380
Is this for real? Hold it, Masayuki!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.090
Are you really giving up after all we've been through?!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.600
This is such a waste!

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.680
We only have 2 more months to go!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.730
You're just freaked out about the Gulf War, right?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.980
Think about it. With your talent, you can be Chief of Staff!

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.610
Thank you, Kohei.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.280
But why?! Didn't you say...

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.650
...you loved being in the Naval Self-Defense Forces?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:03.660
Even if it is justified,

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.910
I still don't want to kill anyone.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.710
You fool!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.880
Japan's not gonna get involved in a war!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.630
Yosuke! Why are you keeping quiet?!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.590
Say something!

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:23.430
This is the decision Masayuki made after some serious thinking.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.140
I can't force him.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.270
So long.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.820
You're such an insensitive person, Yosuke!

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.740
"One man's mistake will endanger the lives of the whole crew."

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.700
"It's unpardonable!"

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.820
Wasn't that what you said?!

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.830
And you call yourself the student leader?!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.450
It's a matter of principle!

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:51.160
Masayuki wanted to be a weapons officer.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.000
I hoped he'd be a weapons officer as well.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:58.420
- And you're just letting him...
- Just let it go!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.130
- What's that?!
- Listen Kohei!

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:02.840
The doors are closing. Please be careful of the closing doors.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.340
That's the decision Masayuki made for himself!

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.840
Oh shut up!

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.970
It's not something we can interfere with!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.180
- Don't you understand!?
- Shut up! Yosuke!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.420
Will the two of you cut that out?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.210
I don't think it's safe...

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:40.260
...to leave the defense of Japan in the hands of you two.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.110
Come on, we're going to miss the curfew.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.420
One minute to impact.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:22.050
I've advised against altering history all along.

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:25.680
However, my hands will soon have blood on them.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.510
With one push of the button, history will now be changed,

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:32.220
and hundreds of lives will be lost.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:35.100
This is the path I have chosen by becoming a weapons officer.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:37.400
And in 40 seconds, I will...

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.400
Even if it is justified,

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.360
I still don't want to kill anyone.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:50.120
Masayuki!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:17.270
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:22.500
Just peacefully

00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:34.280
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:47.190
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:53.800
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:59.870
I kept on praying

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:11.720
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:27.400
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:43.640
I wonder how many men had to go down with the ship.

00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:45.180
Even in Japan there will be...

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:47.480
...those who're opposed to you and the Mirai.

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:49.640
The Mirai's Weapons Officer won't hesitate to take it out.

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:52.810
He won't hesitate when it comes to protecting the Mirai!

00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:55.110
I think you are the one who...

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:57.110
...gave him his "crazy" ideas actually!

00:23:57.110 --> 00:23:59.570
I've killed hundreds with my own hands, and yet...

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:01.780
...it feels like I've just flicked a switch on a video game.

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:05.290
Next Episode: Sinking the Wasp

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:04.410
What the hell is wrong with me?

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:10.170
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
